  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Guests can make a request at the drink counter, and a request card can pass between the drink and cup stations.\", \"decision\": \"How should guests indicate that they want a reusable cup?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nA volunteer gathers reusable-cup requests from waiting guests and takes the cards to both stations. Both stations receive the same choices while guests remain in the queue.\nGuests collect a request card at the cup station and show it when ordering at the drink counter. The cup choice is settled before the drink is prepared.\nGuests request a reusable cup at the drink counter, which sends a request card to the cup station. The cup station prepares for a guest before the guest reaches it."
    }
